WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.470 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.703
-Hey!

00:00:04.703 --> 00:00:06.039
[ Laughs ]

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.041
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.043
It's time for "Corrections."

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.011
We'll just jump right into it,
you guys.

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:15.215
We had a joke in "A Closer Look"
about a note,

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.283
the sort of note you would pass
in high school,

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:22.955
and we spelled "later"
L-8-- the number 8 -- T-E-R.

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:26.793
Many of you pointed out
you wouldn't need the "T,"

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.294
'cause the 8 has a "T" in it.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:32.298
It would be L-8-E-R, would be
the correct way to spell that.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.300
A lot of you said that.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.302
We have learned our lesson,

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:39.305
and, you know,

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:43.309
just a reminder to anyone
who wants to be that nit-picky,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.478
you can go 8 a bag of 6.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.813
Is that right?

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.515
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.719
There's no sailor
in the Village People,

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:57.057
but this is a weird gray area

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.459
because we only said it
as Donald Trump,

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:02.795
and I do think Donald Trump
would think there was a sailor

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.465
in the Village People because of
the song "In the Navy."

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.500
He would hear that
and then just assume

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.503
that maybe all of them
were also sailors,

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:11.837
as sort of a second job.

00:01:11.837 --> 00:01:13.506
People can have two jobs.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:18.010
Also, someone wrote,
according to the cop --

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.511
this is something
a jackal wrote --

00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:23.883
according to the cop,
"YMCA" is just about the YMCA.

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:27.587
Which is probably what,
you know, they told him

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.422
because he was the cop.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.256
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.256 --> 00:01:33.259
You know he said, "Hey, guys,
before we record this,

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.261
I just want to make sure...

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.929
there's no subtext to this,
right?

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:41.934
'Cause, you know, I got a lot
of friends on the force."

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.270
Also, it's crazy.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.607
So nice to be a Republican,

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:51.444
because Trump just walks out

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.947
to gay anthems all the time,

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.783
knowing he's just safe
from criticism.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:00.620
No Democratic politician
would risk

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.789
walking out to "YMCA"
or "Macho Man."

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.625
They would think they'd get
attacked on Fox News

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.961
for -- for weeks!

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:11.230
He's got the -- Donald Trump's
got the same playlist

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.899
as a Pride parade.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.903
Just walking out --
♪ I'm coming out ♪

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:19.572
[ Laughs ]

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:23.442
[As Trump] I think I walk out
to "Born This Way,"

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:27.647
then I talk about how the
American family is under attack,

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.150
and then I exit
to "It's Raining Men."

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:36.122
[Normal voice]
We made a joke about a Prius,

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:39.925
but in the graphic
it was a Subaru Outback.

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:43.663
So of course, I went down
to Graphics and I said,

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.566
"Do you guys know
I wanted a Prius

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.234
and you gave me an Outback?"
And they said,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.404
"Ohh, noooo.

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.406
Are you gonna take us out back?"

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:56.075
[ Muttering ]

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.610
Christ.

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:02.882
We mentioned a law firm
in the Vatican,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.717
a commercial for a law firm
in the Vatican

00:03:05.717 --> 00:03:07.219
where you dial 1-800.

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:10.756
And it was pointed out that
the country code in the Vatican

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:12.091
is 379.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.794
So you would have to dial 379

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.797
if you wanted to call
a lawyer in the Vatican.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.165
And this is interesting.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:23.336
All the attorneys in the Vatican
are defense attorneys.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.605
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.710
Okay.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:36.716
So, this was something
that was sent in...

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:42.221
And this is very hard
for me to read.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:44.523
Because I don't wear glasses.

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:46.059
Oh, there it is. Okay.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.594
So...

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:55.734
We were talking about
how I mixed up Michelangelo

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:59.005
and Da Vinci,
and I sort of said, "Yeah,

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:03.509
but without their bandanas,
how can you tell them apart?"

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:07.079
And someone said, "You said
you couldn't tell them apart

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.414
without their bandanas.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.416
I get that this is a joke
about the Ninja Turtles.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:14.720
However, there is no
Da Vinci Ninja Turtle.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.890
Only a Leonardo.
So the joke falls apart there."

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.059
I would argue

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.562
it fell apart far earlier.

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:25.564
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:28.334
Let's see.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:33.506
Oh, so we talked about
Edvard -- I said "Moonch."

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:36.842
It's pronounced Edvard "Monk."

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:39.178
Edvard Munch.
It's a "K" sound.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.347
And...

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:44.083
And then I did some reading
about Edvard Munch.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.386
He went to the Royal School
of Art and Design in Norway.

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:50.589
He studied in Paris and Berlin.

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:53.426
He suffered from OCD,

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.695
which was very --
which actually made him

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:58.998
very helpful to the local
police department

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:02.334
that would go to him
for his help solving crimes.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.203
They would say, "Get me Munch."

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.540
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:11.844
He was never married.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:15.514
Never married,
and had a girlfriend.

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:17.582
And when he showed her --
it was a heartbreaking story.

00:05:17.582 --> 00:05:19.251
When he showed her...

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:21.386
[ Laughs ]

00:05:21.386 --> 00:05:25.624
When he showed her The Scream,
you know, she just looked at it

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:28.260
and said -- [ Laughs ]

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.095
She goes, "Oh, so you're
the biggest --

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:31.196
You're the -- Ohh --

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:32.698
[ Laughs ]

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:35.234
She's like, "Oh, you're the most
famous Norwegian painter?"

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.737
♪ That don't impress me, Munch ♪

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:39.739
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.109
There was a musical
about his life.

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:45.845
[ Laughing ] It's...

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:49.482
It's true, there was
a musical about his life.

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:52.651
Came out recently.
This is true.

00:05:52.651 --> 00:05:55.021
Called "Dear Edvard."

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:59.191
And critics say --
critics said,

00:05:59.191 --> 00:06:02.228
"If you meant to buy a ticket
for 'Dear Evan Hansen,'

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:04.497
this is the worst
possible outcome."

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:06.165
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.334
"Oh, so much screaming."

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:17.176
I told a joke about
cats with arthritis,

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:20.780
how there was a new treatment
for cats with arthritis,

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.783
which replaced the old treatment

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:26.152
of a brick in a burlap sack.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.455
A lot of cat lovers

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:34.126
were in the comments section
and very upset.

00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:37.129
One went so far to say,
"Can you even imagine?

00:06:37.129 --> 00:06:39.565
Can you imagine telling
that joke about a dog?"

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:42.067
And I would never do that.

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:44.503
You know,
because people like dogs.

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:46.339
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:55.014
We said if there was -- if there
had been voter fraud in Vermont,

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:56.516
Rudy would have done
a press conference

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:58.985
at Burlington Coat Factory.

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:01.620
I was told it's Burlington
Township, New Jersey,

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.956
is why it's the Burlington
Coat Factory.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:08.794
But I think Rudy --
again, artistic license.

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:11.096
I don't think Rudy knows that.

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:13.331
So I think we can
get away with that one.

00:07:13.331 --> 00:07:16.536
We also, though, talked about
Rudy breaking into...

00:07:19.438 --> 00:07:22.708
...the Shawshank prison,
that he would do the reverse.

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:25.544
Andy Dufresne would break out,
and Rudy would break in,

00:07:25.544 --> 00:07:27.513
and he would be happy
because there would be,

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:29.682
you know, a bed and a toilet

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:31.684
and a poster of Rita Hayworth.

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:34.620
Again, multiple jackals
pointed out that

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:38.424
when Andy Dufresne escaped, it
wasn't a Rita Hayworth poster,

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:41.760
it was a Raquel Welch poster.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.364
And one person who said that
followed up by saying,

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:48.000
"I guess you could say
what I've just given you

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.369
is a Shawshank correction."

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:54.674
Leave it to the professionals,
guys.

00:07:54.674 --> 00:07:56.476
[ Laughter ]

00:07:57.976 --> 00:08:00.846
Because that...

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:02.514
don't impress me Munch.

00:08:02.514 --> 00:08:03.950
[ Laughs ]

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:11.023
Oh, so last week's correction,
I talked about a mistake I made,

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:13.025
how I said...

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:14.893
I referred to someone
as a Chewbacca.

00:08:14.893 --> 00:08:17.830
Chewbacca is the name.
Wookie is the species.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:21.400
And then right after that,
right after I clarified that,

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:25.371
I referred to a vampire
as a Dracula.

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:27.907
And many of you said,
"Dude, you just made

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:31.243
the same mistake twice.

00:08:31.243 --> 00:08:33.279
The mistake you just corrected,
you did again."

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:37.283
It's almost like
I did it on purpose.

00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:39.519
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:43.555 --> 00:08:46.558
Oh, we had a joke about --

00:08:46.558 --> 00:08:49.395
there was a tree
named after Leo DiCaprio,

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:51.363
and then we said
it's now dating a sapling.

00:08:51.363 --> 00:08:53.966
And we put up a picture,
but the picture was a seedling,

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:56.502
and I wanted to apologize
and I said I wanted to apologize

00:08:56.502 --> 00:09:01.139
to all the tree enthusiast--
tree enthusiasts.

00:09:01.139 --> 00:09:05.811
And I was told that a word
for tree enthusiasts

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:08.614
is a dendrophile.

00:09:08.614 --> 00:09:13.019
And if you like seedlings,
it's pendrophile.

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:14.887
[ Laughter ]

00:09:16.488 --> 00:09:18.891
And if you want to --
if you are a pendrophile,

00:09:18.891 --> 00:09:22.628
who's looking to talk to some,
you know, like-minded people

00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:24.030
just -- you want
to pick up the phone.

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:26.532
It's, uh, country code 379.

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.501
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.872 --> 00:09:36.275
Did a joke about
the Olive Garden

00:09:36.275 --> 00:09:39.645
and said, "When you're here,
you're family."

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:42.280
That's not Olive Garden's
slogan anymore.

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:45.017
Shoemaker, do you know
whose slogan it is now?

00:09:47.086 --> 00:09:50.289
Jimmy Fallon got the rights
to that slogan.

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:51.957
Do you even remember that?

00:09:51.957 --> 00:09:54.193
He got the rights to it.
They stopped using it.

00:09:54.193 --> 00:09:56.461
The Olive Garden
stopped using it.

00:09:56.461 --> 00:09:58.530
Fallon reached out, said,
"Can we use it?"

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.933
And they gave it to him,
in 2013.

00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:02.334
And so at first I was like,

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:07.673
well, I never got my own slogan,
you know, from a restaurant.

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:09.007
But, you know,
he's "The Tonight Show,"

00:10:09.007 --> 00:10:10.509
and we're "Late Night,"
but then I did the math --

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:11.843
that was when he had
"Late Night."

00:10:11.843 --> 00:10:13.345
So, you know,
I marched up to the brass.

00:10:13.345 --> 00:10:14.847
You know I don't mind
talking to the brass

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:18.517
when I feel as though
I've been slighted.

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:21.220
And I said, you know,
"I want one."

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:26.058
So, you know.

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:27.393
That's -- The problem,
though, of course,

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:29.729
is then you can't be picky
when they get you one.

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:31.630
But we do have a new slogan.

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:34.100
And you'll see it
the next time you see a promo.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.868
If you see like a promo of ours
in "SNL"

00:10:36.868 --> 00:10:38.137
this week after "Update,"

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:40.840
probably right before
good nights, maybe...

00:10:43.275 --> 00:10:46.112
It'll say, you know, it'll say
my guests and whatever,

00:10:46.112 --> 00:10:48.347
and it'll say, you know,
watch this week

00:10:48.347 --> 00:10:49.848
on "Late Night
with Seth Meyers,"

00:10:49.848 --> 00:10:52.785
no one out-pizzas the Hut.

00:10:52.785 --> 00:10:55.087
[ Laughter ]

00:10:58.056 --> 00:11:01.059
I can't be picky.

00:11:01.059 --> 00:11:02.394
They said
it could've been worse.

00:11:02.394 --> 00:11:06.698
I guess the other option
was, "We speak fish."

00:11:06.698 --> 00:11:08.200
It's Long --
[ Laughs ]

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.368
It's Long John S--
[ Laughs ]

00:11:10.368 --> 00:11:12.571
That's Long --
[ Laughs ]

00:11:16.108 --> 00:11:17.309
Thomas Jefferson.

00:11:17.309 --> 00:11:21.480
We talked about Thomas Jefferson
and inventions.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:24.883
I said he invented
the polygraph,

00:11:24.883 --> 00:11:26.418
which was when you --

00:11:26.418 --> 00:11:29.288
It wasn't a lie detector,
but it's two pens attached

00:11:29.288 --> 00:11:31.423
so that when you --
you write in duplicate.

00:11:31.423 --> 00:11:35.094
I guess pantagraph
is technically

00:11:35.094 --> 00:11:36.761
how you would say that.

00:11:36.761 --> 00:11:38.797
And you know, when you look up--
'cause I did, you know,

00:11:38.797 --> 00:11:41.333
I try to do my research
before "Corrections"

00:11:41.333 --> 00:11:43.368
'cause obviously I take it
deeply seriously.

00:11:43.368 --> 00:11:46.905
And a lot of --
some people say Thomas Jefferson

00:11:46.905 --> 00:11:49.108
invented the dumbwaiter
or the pedometer,

00:11:49.108 --> 00:11:51.176
but the more you read,
the more you realize

00:11:51.176 --> 00:11:53.679
he just, like, went --
they had those things in France

00:11:53.679 --> 00:11:55.648
and then he came back
and was like,

00:11:55.648 --> 00:11:59.785
"Look what I invented," but he
just like, bought it there.

00:11:59.785 --> 00:12:03.956
Which sounds like something.
That does sound like something.

00:12:03.956 --> 00:12:07.092
Like, we all respect
Thomas Jefferson so much,

00:12:07.092 --> 00:12:08.827
but that is definitely a thing
you would think

00:12:08.827 --> 00:12:11.897
that Trump would have done,
just like gone abroad

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:13.365
and, like, come back...

00:12:13.365 --> 00:12:15.701
Like, gone to the Middle East
and been like --

00:12:15.701 --> 00:12:18.904
[As Trump]
I've got a new bread.

00:12:18.904 --> 00:12:20.673
It's a circular flatbread.

00:12:23.609 --> 00:12:25.244
It's a pouch.

00:12:29.781 --> 00:12:34.119
[Normal voice] Also, one thing
he brought from Naples --

00:12:34.119 --> 00:12:36.288
it was purchased for
Thomas Jefferson in Naples,

00:12:36.288 --> 00:12:37.956
or as Shoemaker says --
[Italian accent] "Napoli."

00:12:37.956 --> 00:12:39.525
[ Laughs ]

00:12:42.894 --> 00:12:44.530
[ Gibberish ]

00:12:45.664 --> 00:12:47.833
[Normal voice]
It was a macaroni machine,

00:12:47.833 --> 00:12:50.970
and a lot of people say that

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:54.706
Thomas Jefferson popularized
macaroni and cheese

00:12:54.706 --> 00:12:57.909
in the United States
because he got from Naples

00:12:57.909 --> 00:13:01.546
this macaroni machine.

00:13:01.546 --> 00:13:05.217
But, again, he did not invent
macaroni and cheese.

00:13:05.217 --> 00:13:07.219
I think his best --
I think we can all agree

00:13:07.219 --> 00:13:10.089
Thomas Jefferson's
best invention

00:13:10.089 --> 00:13:13.192
was when he had
to invent an excuse

00:13:13.192 --> 00:13:16.528
for why Sally Hemings' kids
had his eyes.

00:13:16.528 --> 00:13:18.097
[ Laughter ]

00:13:20.866 --> 00:13:22.200
'Cause Martha walked in
and was like,

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:23.535
"I have a question."

00:13:23.535 --> 00:13:24.737
He was like,
"I have two questions --

00:13:24.737 --> 00:13:26.739
Do you like macaroni
and cheese?"

00:13:26.739 --> 00:13:28.407
[ Laughter ]

